  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Core Funding to UN Women in support of its 2022 &#x2013; 2025 Strategic Plan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In line with the International Development Strategy and contributing to the delivery of SDG 5, core funding to UN Women supports gender equality and women&#x2019;s empowerment through: encouraging the participation of women in governance and public life; women&#x2019;s economic empowerment; ending violence against women and girls; and women, peace and security, humanitarian action, and disaster risk reduction. UN Women will use the funding to carry out activities under its triple mandate: strengthening global frameworks on gender equality and women&#x2019;s empowerment and translating this into regional and national standards, coordinating across the UN system, and operational activities including at grassroots level in developing countries. Core funding allows UN Women to ensure a gender-lens is applied to the crisis and humanitarian responses of other UN Agencies in a timely manner, and strengthens the capacity of IFIs, the private sector, and civil society on gender equality.</narrative>
  </description>
